WEBVTT

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:44.960
Outta my way!

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:46.760
Hey, get back-

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:53.920
Gotta hurry!

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.840
I can't get this fire going.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.430
One, two, and...

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.430
Good morning!

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.430
Oh... morning.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:48.770
By the way, Mr. Yabuki,

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:51.020
are you in good condition today?

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:52.980
Yeah, I guess so...

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:56.230
Then I suppose your match today with Carlos is in the bag!

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.570
Why don't you give us a V for victory?

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.370
Oh, sure.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:02.570
L-Like this?

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.580
All right, men! Back to work!

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:10.840
Yeah!

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.840
What the hell's going on?

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.050
They're all just nervous.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:18.590
Nervous?

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:23.850
Because... Because your match today is really important to you.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.600
I'm sure they want you to give it your all.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.440
I'm gonna go wash my face.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.190
Right this way!

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:47.660
Right this way!

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.620
Right this way!

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.500
Here, have a rinse.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.560
Here you go!

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.370
Now the only thing left for you to do is go out that door!

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.410
All right, let's get out of here!

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.710
Yeah, let's do that!

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.250
What's the matter, you guys?

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:43.720
Oh, we just figured that Joe would get nervous with us hanging around too long...

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:46.260
And we wanted to be considerate of the fact

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:50.560
that Joe and the old man would want to talk in private before the match...

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.980
So please, continue on with your conversation.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.750
I'll get going, too.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.250
Talking "in private," old man?

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.130
Joe...

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.130
Now that you've come this far,

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:18.090
I have nothing left to say to you.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:20.590
And what's wrong with that?

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.340
If you've got nothing to say, then don't say anything.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:26.060
Joe...

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:27.310
Yeah?

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:31.180
How long has it been since we met at Namida Bridge?

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.440
I've only been able to burn with passion for boxing,

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.400
because you were there.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.770
You made me able to cling on to boxing.

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:46.410
And yet, I couldn't do a single thing for you, except get in your way.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:50.780
So I'm not saying this as your coach or trainer.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.210
I'm saying this as a fan of Yabuki Joe...

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:57.750
A fan of Yabuki Joe who's entrusted him with his tomorrow...

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:58.920
I want you to win!

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.340
Win and cross the Bridge of Tears in the other direction!

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:27.370
I'm really sorry, Joe.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.120
I'm sorry for distracting you with my drivel,

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.580
when you've got an important match coming up.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.830
It's all right, old man.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.580
To tell the truth, I'd be lying if I said I'd never thought that way myself.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.050
But you know, old man...

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:51.270
I hate to admit it, but I'm frozen from nervousness.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:53.940
It takes luck to win.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:59.100
I can't afford to think any other way.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.490
Now then, why don't we get going?

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:08.200
Yeah.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:09.390
You know, old man, I think I might just win.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:11.340
Joe!

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.220
Excuse me! Coming through!

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:14.720
Coming through!

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:15.760
Nishi!

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:19.140
Joe!

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.940
I'm so glad I made it...

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.110
Looks like you've been busy working.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.360
N-No... More importantly,

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.030
I'm sorry I can't be your second for this match,

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.120
but I hope you're fine with me just seeing you off, Joe.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.960
What are you talking about?

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.630
Just work hard at Hayashi's and don't worry about me!

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.080
Thank you, Joe.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.870
Hey, Nishi!

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:49.170
Don't mind the store! I'm closing down for the day, so you go with Joe!

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.880
What are you talking about? We can't afford to...

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:55.890
You didn't hear that! Now go and take care of Joe!

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:00.100
Thanks. Thank you very much, sir.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.990
Well, we've got to do the weigh-in before the match, so we'll go on ahead!

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.140
Joe and Carlos are scheduled to cross gloves at eight tonight.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:37.510
But now I have just one nagging doubt.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:41.060
Joe Yabuki truly is an incredible boxer.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:45.650
That's more than enough reason for me and Carlos to go through with this fight.

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:49.280
But Miss Yohko, you're not a boxer, nor a man.

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:52.530
So why are you so persistent when it comes to Joe?

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.660
I don't know.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:06.000
The only thing I can say is that I feel like I've been fighting him ever since the day we first met.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:12.970
First through Rikiishi-kun, and now through Carlos...

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:17.560
That...

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:20.970
That is the only thing I don't understand.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:29.940
But I feel like today may be the day that it'll all come to an end!

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:06.720
Good evening, ladies and gentlemen! We're here live from Korakuen Hall!

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:12.730
The main event between the world's sixth-ranked bantamweight, Carlos Rivera, and Yabuki Joe

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:14.740
is about to begin!

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:19.440
And talk about a full house today! It's so full, there's almost no room to breathe!

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:30.210
What did he say?

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.630
This fight's gonna last three rounds at best!

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:35.260
But they do call him The Killer...

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:38.840
That's old news!

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:40.930
I'm tellin' ya, Yabuki's not gonna last three rounds!

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:44.730
In fact, I bet he'll barely be able to stand after one!

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:15.580
Well, well... I never expected to see you here, my lady.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:29.270
Thanks to you, I'm able to cross gloves

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:32.060
with a real tough bastard named Carlos tonight.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.150
Thank you.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.980
I'm really grateful for that.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.240
Best of luck, Yabuki-kun.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:11.720
With a pure-white gown on his tanned skin,

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:15.060
Carlos Rivera, the Terror of Venezuela, is making his entrance!

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.860
Having taken down the ranked boxers of Japan in succession,

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:32.580
Carlos Rivera has demonstrated his hard-hitting punches to boxing fans all over Japan!

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:36.290
Just looking at him now, you can tell he's a true boxer!

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:39.960
With his limitless fighting instincts rising up from within,

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:43.590
he appears to be brimming with the wild scent of South America!

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.600
You said it! You're exactly right!

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.580
So, what are your predictions for today's match?

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:51.180
Well, to be perfectly frank...

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.970
And it sounds like his opponent, Yabuki, is making his entrance!

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.610
Ready, and...

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:08.780
Hooray! Hooray! Yabuki!

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:12.700
Hooray! Hooray! Yabuki!

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:16.710
Hooray! Hooray! Yabuki!

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:22.210
Hooray! Hooray! Yabuki!

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:26.220
Hooray! Hooray! Yabuki!

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:33.180
Go for it, Joe!

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:37.150
Well, looks like Yabuki's not lacking in fans! 
There must be two or three hundred of them!

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:41.730
But it does seems that Carlos, 
the non-Japanese, is the more popular one,

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:45.070
but that cheer has really heated up the match!

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:48.070
Back during his debut, Yabuki Joe was even called "The Killer,"

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:52.700
but ever since his match with Rikiishi, he fell so low that he ended up fighting in a grasslot boxing troupe.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:56.170
But today, he challenges the world-ranked Carlos Rivera!

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:58.630
Will this serve as a springboard for his comeback?

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:00.300
Well, I certainly hope so!

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:06.180
Now, by all rights, Yabuki Joe is a wild boxer even greater than Carlos Rivera.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:09.760
Though it's said that Carlos is several ranks above him in terms of technical skills,

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:11.140
we're looking at two wild beasts here.

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:14.560
Perhaps that's why the fans have high hopes for Yabuki.

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:16.520
And the bell's finally about to ring!

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:25.820
Go, Carlos!

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.150
Go full-throttle right from the get-go!

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.150
That's what I plan on doing, Robert.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.530
I'm going to take down Joe Yabuki with everything I have!

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:48.800
Get to a neutral corner!

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:51.390
He took sixteen seconds to KO Tiger,

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:53.060
but only five to KO Yabuki!

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:53.850
1!

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:55.640
2!

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:57.350
3!

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:58.850
Hey, Joe! Get up, dammit!

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:00.850
6!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:02.980
7!

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.410
You're so cool, Bro!

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:16.500
Do it again!

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:19.290
What, you want him to go down again!?

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:20.250
My mistake!

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:23.710
Fight!

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:26.880
That was a nice punch.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:29.250
Now that's how a man oughta punch a man!

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:35.260
Joe!

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.580
Now this doesn't look good. I had high hopes for him,

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:59.620
but there's just too much of a technical gap between them.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.670
B-But Yabuki's just smiling out there!

00:17:01.670 --> 00:17:02.200
He is?

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.890
Y-Yabuki is smiling and laughing,

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:14.550
as if he's enjoying Carlos' punches!

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.560
He's trying to act tough! This isn't good!

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:18.720
And Carlos got him with his left!

00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:25.940
That's his second down!

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:29.690
Yabuki's down for a second time before Carlos' fierce attack!

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:51.630
How long do you plan on counting?

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:54.630
I'm up already.

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:00.640
He's up!

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:16.030
A-And Yabuki's still smiling!

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:20.740
It's like he's stealing Carlos' patented playful smile!

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:22.910
Meanwhile, Carlos is the one with a grave face!

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:27.290
Carlos, I can't help but enjoy myself!

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:30.040
I'm glad I've got you as my opponent.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.050
Joe!

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:40.720
Sorry, Carlos, but I can't afford to take any more punches.

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:43.180
It's about time I made my counterattack!

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:53.940
Now bring it, Carlos!

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:02.700
Wait, Carlos!

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:08.040
This is exactly what happened when you were sparring!

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:08.960
Sparring?

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.460
The Kangaroo Punch...

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:16.460
That's it! Yabuki's waiting for you to throw a straight!

00:19:22.770 --> 00:19:24.390
What's the matter, Carlos?

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:26.140
Why don't you throw a punch?

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:29.940
Now what's the matter with Carlos? Why isn't he punching?

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:33.530
It's because a straightforward attack will be practically begging for Joe's Kangaroo Punch.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:33.530
<i>Kangaroo Punch?</i>

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:36.730
That's right. It's an incredible counter that makes use of the rope's recoil.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:38.440
What's the matter with you?

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.200
What the hell are you waiting for?

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:44.450
D-Does this mean Carlos has run out of ideas?

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:49.450
I'd say so. Any straight knockout punch could make him a victim of the Kangaroo Punch,

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:54.460
but the curvature of the ropes make it easy for him to dodge any small jabs.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:57.760
I see. So Carlos' camp is stumped by Yabuki's strategy!

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:58.930
Idiots!

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:00.380
The hell are you doing?

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:04.550
No, wait!

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:05.550
Oh, right!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.470
There is one way!

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.150
That's it!

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:17.150
A hard swing from the side!

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:19.360
He can't counter that!

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:21.900
Yabuki's up against the wall now!

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:24.740
He did it!

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:11.040
All right!

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:13.660
Way to go!

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.310
Carlos!

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:48.320
Stop!

00:21:54.670 --> 00:21:56.880
Hey, what the hell just happened?

00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:59.330
Carlos just went down instead of Yabuki!

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:05.550
Now this is getting serious!

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:09.010
Carlos, ranked six in the world, the so-called Terror of Venezuela,

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:13.310
has just been knocked down by Yabuki Joe, the champion-elect of Japan!

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:15.310
And we've just got video footage of that scene.

00:22:15.310 --> 00:22:17.690
So this is his swing...

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:20.110
I thought he had him right there.

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:27.620
I figured Carlos was a genius for thinking on his feet in the middle of a fight!

00:22:27.620 --> 00:22:30.240
But then Yabuki's left diverted Carlos' punch!

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:32.280
This is it! That's...

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:39.710
I get it now!

00:22:39.710 --> 00:22:41.710
Now that's amazing!

00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:43.720
That's truly amazing!

00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:47.300
He knocked his recoiling arm against the rope, to use its rebound!

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:51.680
This means Yabuki must've accounted for Carlos throwing a swing!

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:53.480
What a surprise!

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:56.680
Carlos may be a genius, but so is Yabuki!

00:22:57.020 --> 00:22:58.770
Amazing.

00:22:58.770 --> 00:23:01.150
You are an amazing man...

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:03.190
Joe Yabuki...

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:09.200
I guess this means we were right about him, Carlos.

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.500
Yes, exactly right.

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:15.080
Robert, the only thing I can do now

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:19.210
is to follow my instincts and fight to my heart's content!

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:48.420
Joe and Carlos' fight, where they burned fiercely yet beautifully, is over.

00:24:49.300 --> 00:24:52.760
Today, Joe says his farewells to Namida Bridge.

00:24:54.010 --> 00:24:58.020
Today, Joe has survived, and now he lives for tomorrow!

00:24:58.020 --> 00:25:01.860
Let Joe's shining tomorrow burn in the distance!

00:25:02.650 --> 00:25:07.740
Now, as Joe sets forth alone to face his new future,

00:25:07.740 --> 00:25:09.450
which way is tomorrow!?
